**`tasks/cinder-fleet/`** (C-7f8aa502, medium) — Gate-controller firmware dump: TLV parsing, CRC32-validated brute-force of a 4-digit XOR PIN (decoy TOKEN/CRC pairs, CRC-before-TOKEN ordering, noise), then persist `/app/secret.txt` with exact normalization (lowercase, stripped, single trailing newline) plus `/app/pin.txt` and `/app/records.json`. Verifier re-runs `/app/extract.py` on the shipped workspace and 3 hidden dumps (whitespace-padded, mixed-case payloads), byte-checks deliverables against a fresh run, and checks stripped secret contents exactly. Differs from juniper-yonder: no cipher/oracle/C cryptogram chain — firmware TLV + CRC brute force.

Both: `schema_version=1.4`, `verifier_kind=executes-deliverable`, deterministic fixtures, ≥3 hidden cases each, verifier timeout 300s, no network at run/verify; lint clean (the 20 lint errors are pre-existing in unrelated incomplete tasks, untouched). Oracle runs: reward=1.0 for both (sable-marsh needed one fix — pinning numpy/scikit-learn/joblib in its Dockerfile since bench-base lacks them).

